  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting CoCrFeNi alloy is homogeneous and has a single-phase microstructure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Introducing approximately 5–10 vol% Ag is the proposed intervention.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ingot casting followed by thermomechanical processing can produce a fine, uniform dispersion of Ag nano-precipitates in CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dispersed Ag nano-precipitates will segregate and coalesce at the sliding contact surface.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Surface segregation and coalescence of Ag will form a continuous Ag-rich film.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting Ag-rich surface film will be lubricious.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ag has inherently low shear strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ag has favorable oxidation behavior for lubrication at elevated temperatures.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The low shear strength and oxidation behavior of the Ag-rich film will lower friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ag-rich film will reduce adhesive wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ag has a melting point of approximately 961 °C.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ag's melting point and oxidation kinetics will enable a stable lubricious layer from room temperature to 800 °C.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ag-modified alloy will maintain low friction and reduced wear from room temperature to 800 °C in ambient air under an approximately 20 N load.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ag-modified alloy will exhibit roughly a 50% lower coefficient of friction than unmodified CoCrFeNi across the full tested temperature range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ag-modified alloy will have a significantly lower wear rate than unmodified CoCrFeNi across the full tested temperature range.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The optimum Ag fraction and the longevity of the Ag-rich film, especially near 800 °C, are uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
